{{Codex|Drawing from its huge quad-chambered clip, the Tetra is capable of unleashing a sustained barrage of lethal energy bolts.}}

The '''Tetra''' is a {{Faction|Corpus}} assault rifle sporting a large magazine size for sustained fire. The rifle features an average rate of fire and fair accuracy for mid to long range combat.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Puncture}} damage.
*Can use the Tetra-exclusive {{M|Focused Acceleration}} and {{M|Kinetic Ricochet}} mods.

{{Advantages}}

{{Disadvantages|*Projectiles have travel time.}}

{{WeaponComparison|Prisma Tetra}}
{{WeaponComparison|Tenet Tetra}}

==Acquisition==
The Tetra's blueprint can be purchased from the [[Market]].

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}
This weapon can be sold for {{cc|7,500}}.

==Tips==
*With a large portion (80%) of its total damage relying on {{D|Puncture}}, it is somewhat more viable to equip {{M|Piercing Hit}} and/or {{M|Piercing Caliber}} than with most weapons.
**Similarly, because the Tetra has no {{D|Slash}} Damage, {{M|Sawtooth Clip}} and {{M|Fanged Fusillade}} are completely useless.
*With its high recoil, {{M|Stabilizer}} is a good choice to make this weapon more useful at longer ranges.
*While the Tetra has less accuracy than the {{Weapon|Dera}} and weaker overall firepower than the {{Weapon|Supra}}, it deals more damage than the former and has better handling than the latter, making it a good middle-ground weapon in terms of performance. It is also the only Corpus Primary energy weapon whose blueprint can be purchased off the [[Market]], making it more accessible than the clan tech Dera and Supra.
*Third lowest [[fire rate]] of all fully automatic rifles, after {{Weapon|Buzlok}} and {{Weapon|Panthera}}.

==Trivia==
*True to the Tetra's description, the word "Tetra" is a Greek prefix meaning "four"
*The Tetra's battery-like magazines are attached on the muzzle.
**Each of the four "batteries" composes one-fourth of the gun's entire magazine size. Firing up to each quarter (15 rounds by default) round will cause a "battery" to eject.
**All remaining "batteries" will be ejected when reloading manually. The reload animation consists of pushing the stock in, removing the muzzle, and replacing it with a new muzzle complete with fresh batteries before pulling the stock back into place.
*It appears to fire from four distinct barrels, in a clockwise motion, starting at the top right barrel and ending at the top left.

